  (text "J2 -> SW2: 1 = 12 V in (switch power terminal),\n2 = 12 V out (switch load terminal), 3 = lamp GND.\nJ3 -> valve: 1 = valve +, 2 = valve -. Valve flyback\ndiode D2 is on the board." (at 115.57 238.76 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 2cb3ea4d-fab7-5576-9b21-a564b9368716)
  )
  (text "INTERFERENCE AND RELIABILITY MEASURES" (at 279.4 182.88 0)
    (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid c1b5f376-481c-57c7-b668-a0bac5b48132)
  )
  (text "1. D2 flyback diode at the valve output; Q1 switches the valve + (high side), valve - goes to GND.\n2. 2 mm tracks for the 12 V and valve current; GND poured on both layers.\n3. Decoupling: C1 + C2 on 12 V, C3 + C4 at U1, C10 at the Nano, C6 at J3.\n4. Flow input: R1 10k pull-up, R2 1k + C5 10nF filter, firmware glitch filter.\n5. Button: R3 10k + C7 100nF. Remote: R7-R10 1k series, R13-R16 100k pull-downs,\n   receiver supply filtered by R17 + C8 + C9. Firmware debounces both.\n6. F1 fuse (before the main switch) + D1 crowbar protect against shorts and a reversed supply.\n7. R11 / R12 divide the 5 V data line to 3.2 V for the ESP; R21 protects D12 from the ESP.\n8. Twist the flow sensor signal with its GND; route it away from the valve and 12 V wires.\n9. Receiver antenna end at a board edge, away from the valve driver and the regulator." (at 279.4 186.69 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 4db31949-b272-5bea-868d-10d4a3f26a80)
  )

  (sheet_instances
